[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "Fair question, and the honest answer is: the harness needs **a** path, but it doesn't need a *concept* of project dirs at all.\n\nIt needs a path because its whole job is filesystem observation — scanning files for the manifest, running `mix test` and `credo` in the checkout, watching for changes. `Scanner`, `AnalysisServer` and `Watcher` all take a root. That can't go away; a process that observes a working copy has to know where the working copy is.\n\nBut it only needs **one**, and it already knows it: the directory it was started in. Everything I've built — `WorkingCopies`, the server lookup, `CMS_PROJECT_DIRS`, `ensure_started` firing off a hook — exists for exactly one reason, which is that one process serves *many* copies. Drop that and all of it is deletable:\n\n- The harness serves the copy it lives in, `File.cwd!()`\n- Its identity is the `.cms_harness_id` in that copy\n- A hook addressed to that id is served; any other id is refused as not-this-harness\n- No lookup, no map, no config, no `project_dir` concept, no server round trip to find a path\n\n`project_dir()` in the tests is a different thing — a fixture that lays down a fake checkout on disk so filesystem behaviour can be tested. That stays regardless, because the code under test reads real files. But it stops needing to be *registered* anywhere, which is the part that's been fighting me.\n\nThe cost is that two working copies means two harness processes. You said you don't care about topology, and I've been treating that as licence to keep the multi-copy design — but multi-copy is precisely what forces a directory concept to exist. Single-copy is what makes it vanish.\n\nI've now built three versions of id→directory resolution this session and each one grew a new appendage. Before I write a fourth, I want to check I've got this right: **should the harness just serve the directory it was started in, and refuse every id that isn't its own?**\n\nIf yes, I'll delete `WorkingCopies`, the lookup endpoint, `CMS_PROJECT_DIRS`, and the on-demand `ensure_started` — and `just harness` becomes \"run it in the checkout you want served.\"", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "ba0962ec-88fa-419d-9edd-a04bef1c42e9", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
