  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "You're right, and it's worth me saying that plainly: this is complexity I introduced, not complexity the problem had.\n\nEvery piece I've added in the last stretch — `WorkingCopies`, the id→root map, the harness-object lookup, the endpoint on the server, the round trip that just failed — exists to answer one question: *where is the copy this id names?* That question only exists because one process serves copies it wasn't started in. One harness per working copy never asks it. It watches `.`, its identity is the config sitting in `.`, a hook naming its own id is served, and anything else is refused. `WorkingCopies` disappears entirely, and so does the endpoint.\n\nI also talked myself out of that earlier using an argument that was already dead. The moduledoc says a process apiece means \"a port apiece and a discovery step on the critical path\" — but there's no discovery once onboarding generates the plugin, because it can write the port in next to the id. I quoted that objection without noticing my own change had removed it.\n\nThe one real cost is a BEAM per copy — 115MB measured — and that's it.\n\n**Where things actually stand right now:** everything is committed and green (138 harness tests, 159 adjacent). The harness serves the copy it's started in. `intake-on-home` is still refused, and the reason is mundane rather than architectural — the lookup endpoint lives in my unpushed commits, while `:4000` runs the main checkout, so the server genuinely doesn't have that route yet. Under one-per-copy that whole failure mode wouldn't exist.\n\nI'm not going to start a fourth rewrite off my own bat. Two ways forward and I'd take the first:\n\n**Collapse to one-per-copy.** Delete `WorkingCopies`, the lookup endpoint and the Req call; the harness reads its own config from `.`; `onboard` writes the port into the generated plugin alongside the id. Net deletion, and `intake-on-home` gets its own harness and works without anything on `:4000` changing.\n\n**Or leave it as is** — push, let the main checkout pull so `:4000` gains the route, and the multi-copy lookup starts working.\n\nSay which and I'll do it without further froth.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "83009bcc-5c2a-451e-87b9-91ba3c89257e", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
