  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/phx-new-generator", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "6bc4851f-f735-4590-bb1c-c660619b4019", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "Nothing in the harness reads the payload's `cwd` — so **as far as the harness is concerned, no.** The plugin dir is an absolute path and every URL in it carries the id, so a session launched from anywhere reaches the right working copy. That's the whole point of what we just built; I verified it repeatedly by sending `cwd: /tmp` and still getting the right copy's answer.\n\n**Two caveats, and they're both about Claude Code rather than the harness.**\n\n`just claude-dev` specifically must be run from that checkout, because `justfile_directory()` resolves to wherever the justfile lives. Run it from my worktree and you'd get my `plugin-dev` and my id. The explicit `claude --plugin-dir /abs/path` form has no such constraint.\n\nAnd Claude Code's own working directory still decides what the *agent* sees — which files it can read and edit, which `.claude/settings.json` applies, what `git` commands act on. So you'd start it in the worktree you want it working in for ordinary reasons, not harness ones.\n\nPractically: start it in the worktree, because that's where you want it working. But if it somehow launched from elsewhere with the right `--plugin-dir`, the harness would still attribute everything correctly — the id in the URL is the only thing that decides.", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "e196cc0c-c9ee-43f1-acc8-4e93d9a7e3bf", "session_crons" => [], "session_id" => "80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37", "stop_hook_active" => false, "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec--claude-worktrees-phx-new-generator/80dcd471-007d-4438-8f86-f511c41e6e37.jsonl"}
