[debug] Processing with CmsHarness.Web.HooksController.handle/2
  Parameters: %{"cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/intake-on-home", "duration_ms" => 6, "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "d1c8f8f5-13e5-4827-865e-55a081f988a6", "hook_event_name" => "PostToolUse", "permission_mode" => "auto", "prompt_id" => "6538f045-2dac-4de2-a0a7-4dbe1f3c3506", "session_id" => "9703aaca-90cf-4469-8202-6146afe86064", "tool_input" => %{"file_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec/memory/project_no_auto_provisioning.md"}, "tool_name" => "Read", "tool_response" => %{"file" => %{"content" => "---\nname: No auto-provisioning of accounts; no \"personal account\" concept\ndescription: Account creation is a manual onboarding step; \"personal account\" was removed project-wide\ntype: project\noriginSessionId: d3042690-0987-42b8-a37f-8f096e90412e\n---\nTwo related constraints when restoring/authoring BDD for any auth or onboarding story:\n\n1. **No auto-provisioning of accounts.** When a user signs in for the first time via magic link or OAuth callback, the auth flow does NOT create an account for them automatically. Account creation is a separate manual step in the /app onboarding wizard (story 606). Do not write rules or scenarios that have the callback/magic-link provision an account, membership, or active-account preference.\n\n2. **No \"personal account\" concept.** There is no longer a distinct \"personal account\" entity or first-account-is-personal default. Accounts are just accounts. Don't write rules about \"creating a personal account\", \"healing legacy users without a personal account\", or \"pre-selecting the personal account as active\".\n\n**Why:** Confirmed during 2026-05-12 BDD restoration of stories 601 + 602. The user explicitly removed the personal-account concept and the auto-provisioning behavior. The commit `46a1c417 Activation funnel polish + generic events + drop personal-account concept` is the canonical reference.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Story 601 (magic link): 3 rules — log in without confirmation screen, idempotent re-click, expired links don't log in. No 4th rule about provisioning.\n- Story 602 (OAuth callback): 5 rules — confirmed user, integration row persisted, idempotent sign-in, email-required, integration-save-failure doesn't gate login. No 6th rule about personal-account flow.\n- Story 606 (account creation wizard) is the home for \"user manually creates their first account\" scenarios — don't duplicate that intent into 601/602.\n- When pre-migration criteria descriptions mention \"personal account\", remove or rephrase to just \"account\".\n", "filePath" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec/memory/project_no_auto_provisioning.md", "numLines" => 20, "startLine" => 1, "totalLines" => 20}, "type" => "text"}, "tool_use_id" => "toolu_01JQTcNneXrVuQvGApRWPXX6", "transcript_path" => "/Users/johndavenport/.claude/projects/-Users-johndavenport-Documents-github-code-my-spec/9703aaca-90cf-4469-8202-6146afe86064.jsonl"}
