  Parameters: %{"background_tasks" => [], "cwd" => "/Users/johndavenport/Documents/github/code_my_spec/.claude/worktrees/intake-on-home", "effort" => %{"level" => "xhigh"}, "harness_id" => "d1c8f8f5-13e5-4827-865e-55a081f988a6", "hook_event_name" => "Stop", "last_assistant_message" => "That false-positived on a session id — nothing about story 990.\n\n**Honest answer: memory holds no outstanding onboarding work.** It has exactly one onboarding entry, and it's a *constraint*, not a task:\n\n**No auto-provisioning of accounts** (87 days old) — signing in via magic link or OAuth must not create an account; that's a manual step in the `/app` wizard (story 606). Also, no \"personal account\" concept. It's guidance for writing BDD on auth/onboarding stories, and it's still worth honoring — though it's old enough that I'd verify against the code before treating any file reference in it as current.\n\n**The real outstanding onboarding item isn't in memory — it's from this session**, and it's what this worktree is named for: moving the guided intake from `/build` onto the index/home page. You said *\"ultimately it's supposed to go on the index/home.\"* Nothing's been done on it — `intake-on-home` has zero commits.\n\nIt wouldn't be in memory by design; your standing rule is no plans in memory, use plan mode.\n\nEverything else onboarding-related from this session is closed: all five QA issues resolved against story 990, the plugin rung and \"Open the local workspace\" rung removed from `/app`, and the nav gate that was hiding the menu from people who had a project.\n\nTwo things I could pick up now:\n\nThe **intake-on-home** work itself — though when I checked, `/` returned no `<h1>` my grep caught, so I'd want to read what the marketing page is actually built from before proposing how the intake slots in.\n\nOr the smaller one I offered: appending today's `list_projects` finding to `framework_issue_auth_url_404.md`, since it's the same message giving the same dead URL for a